This has ideas about porting Super ZZ Zero to other systems. It also
includes notes about possible new or changed user configuration options.


=== GNU/Linux ===

Super ZZ Zero is already designed for GNU/Linux systems, although it might
be helpful to be included in package managers of some distributions.

Some systems may use SDL2 or SDL3 instead of SDL1, especially if the system
is using Wayland. Compatibility layers exist, but its use may need testing.


=== DOS ===

DOS has 8.3 case-insensitive file names. This should not be a problem with
most of the working of Super ZZ Zero.

The save/restore game menu might have to be changed somewhat, but still
mostly retaining the existing UI, to work with DOS file names properly.

The user configuration file will need to have a different name, and will
probably be stored in the same directory as the executable file.

audio_music_driver
  Specify the sound driver for music lumps (not currently implemented).
  (It can also read settings from the BLASTER environment variable.)

audio_pc_driver
  Specify the sound driver for PC sound effects (#PLAY and SFX), such as
  using the PC speaker directly (which will disable the volume controls),
  or emulated using some sound card.

audio_wave_driver
  Specify the sound driver for wave sounds (not currently implemented).

copy_current_font
  If set to 1 then it enables the function to allow copying the current
  text mode font into the world file. This only works if the video mode
  is set to a suitable text mode.

help
  In DOS, if this option is not specified, it will look in the subdirectory
  of the directory with the executable file. (You can still override it
  with your own specification if you want to do.)

joy_calibration
  Sets the calibration setting for joysticks.

joy_type
  Specifies the joystick type, which can be "PC" (only two buttons and two
  axes), "GRAVIS" (has four buttons), or "GRAVIS_PRO" (which has many more
  buttons as well, and up to four controllers).

printer_port
  Specify the port that the printer is connected to, such as "LPT1". (If
  it is connected to a PostScript printer, you must use the printer_begin
  option to specify the name of a file containing a ESC/P emulator written
  in PostScript, and printer_end with whatever is used to terminate it.)
  Specify "FILE:" and a file name if you want to print to file.

show_status
  This setting is only meaningful with some video modes; it is not
  meaningful in text mode.

video_mode
  Specifies preferred and acceptable video modes.

The following configuration settings are not meaningful on DOS:
  full_screen
  joy_name
  time_utc


=== Windows ===

Windows also has case-insensitive file names like DOS has; this probably
does not require any changes to Super ZZ Zero. However, another feature
of file names in Windows is that they will normally use Unicode; this
will not work with Super ZZ Zero unless native_file_picker is used (see
the below description), but file names with only ASCII characters can
still be displayed and used. If the PC character set is in use though,
then it can be used directly.

It will probably also be appropriate on Windows to allow user settings to
be stored in the registry. Windows registry has several data types. For
Super ZZ Zero, different options have different types (although the text
configuration file always stores them as text). REG_SZ and REG_EXPAND_SZ
would be suitable for file names and for other text that is used with
Windows API functions. REG_DWORD (and sometimes REG_QWORD) would be used
for integer values and for boolean values. Other settings would probably
use REG_BINARY, but would also allow REG_SZ and REG_EXPAND_SZ if the string
is limited to only ASCII characters.

Windows also has file associations in the Explorer and File Manager, and
allows multiple menu options, so it can include menus for "play" and for
"edit", so that if a file is right-clicked you can select the function.

There is also COM automation, which also might have some use.

A built-in option menu for configuration by GUI might also be suitable.

joy_guid
  Specifies the DirectX instance GUID for the joystick.

menu_bar
  Enables or disables the menu bar. You cannot push F10 to select the menu
  bar, but you can push ALT by itself to select the menu bar, if the menu
  bar is enabled.

native_file_picker
  If set to 1 then the save/restore game menu will use the Windows file
  dialog boxes instead of the built-in UI of Super ZZ Zero.

native_text_edit
  If set to 1 then the text editing widget of Windows is used instead of
  the built-in UI of Super ZZ Zero.

printer_type
  Specify W to display the Windows printing dialog box when F11 is pushed.
  This will then be used to print using the functions of Windows.

renderer
  Specifies the type of renderer to use.

time_format
  If not specified, it uses the date/time format setting in Windows.

time_format_mode
  Selects to use short or long date/time formats.


=== Mac OS X ===

I do not know much about it. However, there are a few things. The command
key is not used in Super ZZ Zero, but an implementation on Mac OS X can
use it for the common functions that it is used for with its combinations,
such as Command+Q to quit, Command+P to print, etc.

Mac OS X also uses UTI. The UTI for a Super ZZ Zero world file should be
"org.zzo38computer.superzz0.world", and this conforms to the UTI for the
Hamster archive format, which is "com.hamsterrepublic.lumped".

Some functions of Windows such as a configuration menu would also be
possible on Mac OS X, too.

AppleScript is another thing; it might be possible to make it possible
to work some functions (e.g. board editor automation) with AppleScript,
but because it uses Unicode, it will not be possible to work properly
with non-Unicode text.

native_file_picker
  Like on Windows.

native_text_edit
  Like on Windows.

time_format_mode
  Selects to use short or long date/time formats.


=== A currently unnamed operating system design ===

Command, Automation, and Query Language may be usable to command, automate,
and query the Super ZZ Zero.

The .CCM lumps would probably be used with this system, since they can be
used to interoperate text with other programs; it would also be usable to
allow the application to tell the keyboard manager which input character
set it wants, to automatically set the IME by the context. (This is not
possible in most other systems since they use Unicode, but this one uses
TRON code, which is better.)

In this system, many settings that refer to files and directories will
not work as is; the values will be links to the files instead. Settings
that refer to external programs will need to refer to capabilities. For
directories (only "help" so far), the link would usually be to a file with
a key/value list, which associates the names (in ASCII) to the files.

full_screen
  This is not available. If you want to use full screen, you must use the
  facilities of the operating system to display it as full screen, which
  is a separate setting from the application-specific configuration.

native_text_edit
  Like on Windows.

printer_type
  This can be set to W to use the operating system's printing functions.

time_format
  If not specified, the locale setting will be used (which also makes it
  possible to use non-Gregorian calendars), if it can be used with the
  current character set. This setting is ignored if Super ZZ Zero does
  not have permission to determine the current date and time.

time_format_mode
  Selects to use short or long date/time formats.

The following configuration settings are not meaningful:
  auto_suffix
  file_list
  full_screen
  joy_index
  joy_name
  save_dir

(Such things as joypad selections and full screen are handled by other
software on the system and does not need to be configured by the
application programs, so such settings are not used by Super ZZ Zero.
The button/axis mapping still needs to be configured in Super ZZ Zero.)


=== HTML ===

One possible feature is to allow automation of some editor functions using
JavaScripts (like it would be possible using AppleScript on Mac OS X).

joy_name
  When using HTML, the joy_name is the "id" property of the Gamepad object.
  If it does not match any of them exactly, it is a prefix.

js_time_format
  Specifies the JSON data which will be decoded and used as the options for
  the Intl.DateTimeFormat. (This will not work within the user interface of
  Super ZZ Zero itself unless the resulting format uses only ASCII
  characters, but can still be used in other interfaces.)

native_text_edit
  Like on Windows.

The following configuration settings are not meaningful on HTML:
  auto_suffix
  extra_lump_file
  extra_lump_name
  file_list
  help
  printer_begin
  printer_command
  printer_end
  printer_type
  save_dir
  test_mode
  text_editor_command

